2025-05-01 02:56:27 - Thread-1089 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns & why they matter  
• `fullVisitorId` : visitor identifier – lets us count unique visitors or purchasers  
• `totals.transactions` : number of transactions in that session – if NOT NULL (and normally > 0) the visitor is a purchaser; also needed to average transactions

Typical filter / grouping conditions  
• `WHERE totals.transactions IS NOT NULL` — keep only sessions with a purchase  
• `GROUP BY fullVisitorId` — aggregate sessions that belong to the same visitor  
• `HAVING SUM(totals.transactions) > 0` — be sure the visitor really bought something  

Below are ten exploratory–to–final BigQuery queries (all limited to ≤ 20 rows) that progressively surface the information required.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at raw data: visitor id and session‑level transactions
SELECT
  fullVisitorId,
  totals.transactions
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show only sessions where at least one transaction occurred
SELECT
  fullVisitorId,
  totals.transactions
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
WHERE totals.transactions IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Distinct list of visitors present in the table
SELECT DISTINCT
  fullVisitorId
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Distinct list of purchasers (visitors with ≥1 transaction in ≥1 session)
SELECT DISTINCT
  fullVisitorId
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
WHERE totals.transactions IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count total number of unique visitors (conversion denominator)
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT fullVisitorId) AS total_unique_visitors
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Count total number of unique purchasers (conversion numerator)
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT fullVisitorId) AS total_unique_purchasers
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
WHERE totals.transactions IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Calculate conversion rate from visitors to purchasers
SELECT
  SAFE_DIVIDE(
    COUNT(DISTINCT IF(totals.transactions IS NOT NULL, fullVisitorId, NULL)),
    COUNT(DISTINCT fullVisitorId)
  ) AS conversion_rate
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Aggregate transactions per purchaser so we can average later
SELECT
  fullVisitorId,
  SUM(totals.transactions) AS total_transactions_by_visitor
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
WHERE totals.transactions IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY fullVisitorId
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Average number of transactions per purchaser
WITH purchaser_tx AS (
  SELECT
    fullVisitorId,
    SUM(totals.transactions) AS total_tx
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
  WHERE totals.transactions IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY fullVisitorId
)
SELECT
  AVG(total_tx) AS avg_transactions_per_purchaser
FROM purchaser_tx
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: conversion rate & average transactions per purchaser in one shot
WITH
  visitors AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
  ),
  purchasers AS (
    SELECT
      fullVisitorId,
      SUM(totals.transactions) AS transactions_per_visitor
    FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics`
    WHERE totals.transactions IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY fullVisitorId
  )
SELECT
  -- visitors & purchasers
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM purchasers)                     AS unique_purchasers,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM visitors)                       AS unique_visitors,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(
    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM purchasers),
    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM visitors)
  )                                                     AS conversion_rate,
  AVG(transactions_per_visitor)                         AS avg_transactions_per_purchaser
FROM purchasers
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query isolates a different aspect of the data, culminating in query 10 which produces the required metrics directly from the `data-to-insights.ecommerce.web_analytics` table.
